{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790419733211,"sessionID":"ses_f22acadb8ffeibdBLJ0SrsnIn0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_6c05e56b361a4839b5f883d9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore existing project","prompt":"Explore the /workspace project directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The contents of project.godot\n2. The scenes/ directory structure\n3. The scripts/ directory structure\n4. The global/ directory structure\n5. The task_config.json contents\n6. Any existing .gd scripts to understand coding conventions (especially look for an Events autoload or singleton pattern)\n7. Any existing .tscn files to understand structure conventions\n\nReturn ALL file contents and directory listings you find. Be very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f22ac559bffeW80SQIw4Bb3Wu8\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a complete and thorough report of everything found in the `/workspace` project directory.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `/workspace/project.godot` (Full Contents)\n\n```\n; Engine configuration file.\n; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Battle Over Panel Task\"\nconfig/description=\"Create a battle over screen with buttons and logic\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[autoload]\n\nEvents=\"*res://global/events.gd\"\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n\n**Key takeaways:**\n- **Project name:** \"Battle Over Panel Task\"\n- **Description:** \"Create a battle over screen with buttons and logic\"\n- **Main scene:** `res://scenes/main.tscn`\n- **Autoloads:** Exactly one -- `Events`, registered at `*res://global/events.gd` (the `*` means it is globally available as a singleton named `Events`)\n- **Rendering:** `gl_compatibility` (Godot 4.4)\n- **Config version:** 5\n\n---\n\n## 2. `scenes/` Directory Structure\n\n```\n/scenes/\n  main.tscn          (the only file)\n```\n\nThe `scenes/` directory has **no subdirectories**. It contains a single file:\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` (Full Contents)\n\n```\n[gd_scene format=3 uid=\"uid://d1011main\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node\"]\n```\n\nThis is a minimal Godot 4 scene file. It contains exactly one root node:\n- **Node name:** `Main`\n- **Type:** `Node` (the base Godot `Node` type, no derived class)\n- **UID:** `uid://d1011main`\n- **Scene format version:** 3\n\nThere are **no existing `.gd` scripts** attached to this scene.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `scripts/` Directory Structure\n\n```\n/scripts/\n  (empty directory -- zero files)\n```\n\nThe `scripts/` directory exists but is **completely empty**. No GDScript files exist here at all.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `global/` Directory Structure\n\n```\n/global/\n  events.gd           (script file)\n  events.gd.uid       (Godot UID file)\n```\n\n### `/workspace/global/events.gd` (Full Contents)\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nsignal battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: int)\n```\n\n**Key takeaways:**\n- **Extends:** `Node`\n- **Defines one signal:** `battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: int)`\n- **No class_name** -- this script does not declare itself as a named class.\n- **No other methods** or variables are defined.\n- This is the **Events autoload/singleton** -- it is registered in `project.godot` as `Events=\"*res://global/events.gd\"`, meaning it is accessible globally as `Events` from any script.\n- The signal takes two parameters:\n  - `text: String` -- the message to display on the battle over screen\n  - `type: int` -- an integer representing the result type (likely `0` = WIN, `1` = LOSE, or vice versa)\n\n### `/workspace/global/events.gd.uid` (Full Contents)\n\n```\nuid://ct11hvse5mkj0\n```\n\nStandard Godot UID file for the events script.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `task_config.json` (Full Contents)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Create a battle over UI panel scene and its script. Add res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.tscn with a root Panel named BattleOverPanel, set process mode to Always, and stretch it to full rect. Override the panel style with a StyleBoxFlat using rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34902). Add a centered VBoxContainer with offsets -20/-20/20/20. Inside it, add a Label named Label with text \\\"Victorious!\\\", centered horizontal and vertical alignment, and LabelSettings font_size 24. Add two Buttons named ContinueButton and RestartButton, each with custom_minimum_size (50, 16), size_flags_horizontal set to expand fill, and texts \\\"Awesome!\\\" and \\\"Restart\\\" respectively. Create res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.gd that class_names BattleOverPanel, defines enum Type {WIN, LOSE}, binds the Label and both Buttons with % paths, connects ContinueButton to get_tree().quit and RestartButton to get_tree().reload_current_scene in _ready, and connects Events.battle_over_screen_requested to show_screen. Implement show_screen(text, type) to update the label text, toggle ContinueButton for WIN and RestartButton for LOSE, show the panel, and pause the scene tree.\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is the task specification. It describes exactly what needs to be created. I'll summarize the requirements for clarity:\n\n**Scene file:** `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.tscn`\n- Root is a `Panel` node named `BattleOverPanel`\n  - Process mode: `Always`\n  - Stretch to full rect (anchors to all corners, margins at 0)\n  - Panel style override: `StyleBoxFlat` with `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34902)` (semi-transparent black)\n- Child: centered `VBoxContainer` with offsets `(-20, -20, 20, 20)`\n  - Child: `Label` named `Label` with text `\"Victorious!\"`, centered alignment, `LabelSettings` with `font_size = 24`\n  - Child: `Button` named `ContinueButton` -- text `\"Awesome!\"`, `custom_minimum_size = (50, 16)`, `size_flags_horizontal = expand fill`\n  - Child: `Button` named `RestartButton` -- text `\"Restart\"`, `custom_minimum_size = (50, 16)`, `size_flags_horizontal = expand fill`\n\n**Script file:** `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.gd`\n- `class_name BattleOverPanel`\n- Defines `enum Type {WIN, LOSE}`\n- Binds `Label`, `ContinueButton`, `RestartButton` using `%` unique name paths\n- In `_ready`:\n  - Connect `ContinueButton.pressed` to `get_tree().quit`\n  - Connect `RestartButton.pressed` to `get_tree().reload_current_scene`\n  - Connect `Events.battle_over_screen_requested` to `show_screen`\n- `show_screen(text, type)` method:\n  - Updates the label text to the passed `text`\n  - Shows `ContinueButton` if type is `WIN`, hides `RestartButton`\n  - Shows `RestartButton` if type is `LOSE`, hides `ContinueButton`\n  - Shows the panel\n  - Pauses the scene tree (`get_tree().paused = true`)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Coding Conventions (GDScript)\n\n### Existing `.gd` scripts:\n\n**`/workspace/global/events.gd`:**\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nsignal battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: int)\n```\n\nConventions observed:\n- **File naming:** Lowercase snake_case (`events.gd`)\n- **No shebang** or header comment\n- **`extends Node`** on the first line\n- **Blank line** between `extends` and signal definition\n- **Signal naming:** snake_case (`battle_over_screen_requested`)\n- **Parameter typing:** Statically typed signal parameters (`text: String, type: int`)\n- **Trailing newline** at end of file\n\n### Autoload / Singleton Pattern:\n\n- Registered in `project.godot` under `[autoload]` as `Events=\"*res://global/events.gd\"`\n- The `*` prefix means it is enabled as a global autoload singleton\n- Other scripts access it directly as `Events` (e.g., `Events.battle_over_screen_requested.connect(...)`)\n- The autoload script lives in `/workspace/global/` directory\n\n---\n\n## 7. Scene File Conventions (`.tscn`)\n\n**`/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`:**\n```\n[gd_scene format=3 uid=\"uid://d1011main\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node\"]\n```\n\nConventions observed:\n- **Scene format version:** 3 (Godot 4.x)\n- **UID:** Standard Godot resource UID format (`uid://...`)\n- **Node declaration:** `[node name=\"Name\" type=\"Type\"]`\n- **Node hierarchy:** Simple flat structure, one root node\n- **No scripts attached** to the scene (no `script = ExtResource(...)` line)\n- **Trailing newline**\n\n### `.godot/` Directory (Internal Godot Cache)\n\nFor completeness:\n\n| Path | Contents |\n|------|----------|\n| `.godot/.gdignore` | Empty file (tells Godot to ignore this directory as a resource) |\n| `.godot/uid_cache.bin` | Binary file (resource UID cache) |\n| `.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg` | `list=[]` (no global script classes registered) |\n| `.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg` | Empty file (no scene groups) |\n| `.godot/editor/project_metadata.cfg` | Editor path: `/run/gamedevbench-bin/godot`, recent scenes: `res://scenes/main.tscn` |\n| `.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10` | Filesystem cache listing all project files with metadata |\n| `.godot/editor/main.tscn-folding-3ad5...cfg` | Folding data (all empty arrays) |\n| `.godot/imported/` | Empty directory (no imported assets) |\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a **Godot 4.4 project** with a single, focused purpose: to create a \"Battle Over\" UI panel. The project has:\n\n- **1 autoload singleton:** `Events` (`/workspace/global/events.gd`) -- exposes `battle_over_screen_requested(text, type)` signal\n- **1 scene:** `main.tscn` -- a bare `Node` root with no logic attached\n- **1 empty directory:** `scripts/` -- awaiting scripts\n- **1 task specification:** `task_config.json` -- describes the UI panel and script to create at `scenes/ui/`\n- **No existing `class_name` registrations** (global_script_class_cache is empty)\n- **Uses `%` unique name paths** for node binding (per the task instructions)\n- **Signals use static typing** for parameters\n- **Events autoload is globally available** as `Events`\n</